## Report
Dynamic attempts: `cargo build -p server` failed due to crates.io access (403), and `cargo build --offline` failed because `tiny_http` was not cached. valgrind and gdb are not installed, so crash/valgrind/debugger validation could not proceed. Code review shows anonymous access is allowed when auth headers are missing (AuthContext::Anonymous on MissingAuth in crates/server/src/http/mod.rs:307-334). Authorization helpers call `self.coordinator.head_bucket(bucket)?` before checking permissions (crates/server/src/http/mod.rs:373-396), and dispatch uses these helpers for bucket operations (e.g., HeadBucket/ListObjects in crates/server/src/http/mod.rs:93-105). The coordinator maps missing buckets to `ServerError::BucketNotFound` (crates/server/src/coordinator.rs:236-239), and ServerError maps BucketNotFound to NoSuchBucket/HTTP 404 while auth errors map to AccessDenied/HTTP 403 (crates/server/src/error.rs:57-92). Thus an unauthenticated caller can distinguish existing private buckets (403) from non-existent ones (404), confirming the enumeration issue.

